>>
Rule 1 (input tensor must have a defined number of dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 2 (each dimension size must be non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 3 (if the tensor has at least one dimension, the first dimension size is valid)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 then shape(v_1, 0) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (scalar tensors are allowed)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 0 ∨ ndim(v_1) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 5 (input tensor’s dtype must be well-defined)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_1)
